4. Include VERIQTA publications in paid courses, bootcamps, workshops, subscription communities, training packages, or commercial educational products.

5. Modify, adapt, translate, abridge, rebrand, or create derivative versions of protected materials for redistribution or publication.

6. Remove, conceal, modify, or replace copyright notices, ownership information, author credits, watermarks, logos, or licensing statements.

7. Present VERIQTA materials as independently authored, jointly authored, institutionally owned, or officially endorsed by another individual or organization.

8. Compile, package, mirror, or distribute substantial portions of this repository as an alternative educational collection.

9. Incorporate protected materials into commercial textbooks, digital products, educational platforms, or downloadable resource bundles without authorization.

10. Use protected materials as training, fine-tuning, evaluation, or retrieval datasets for artificial intelligence or machine-learning systems without prior written authorization, except where applicable law independently permits such use.

11. Systematically scrape, harvest, or reproduce the repository for the purpose of creating unauthorized copies, competing content libraries, or redistribution platforms.

12. Grant third parties rights over VERIQTA intellectual property.

The absence of a purchase price, public GitHub availability, or an accessible download option does not constitute authorization for these activities.


